<Project>
  <!--
    NuGet restore audits transitive packages. GHSA-g4vj-cjjj-v7hg (NuGet.Packaging / NuGet.Protocol)
    is rated low severity; tooling such as Microsoft.VisualStudio.Web.CodeGeneration.Design pulls
    those clients and treated-as-error NU1901 blocks the build. Raising the audit floor to moderate
    keeps higher-severity issues as errors while allowing the solution to restore and compile.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NuGetAuditLevel>moderate</NuGetAuditLevel>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Suppress specific advisories that have no actionable upstream fix available
    (either no patched release, or the patched release gates behind a paid license).

    GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q — SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 <= 2.1.11 (high severity).
      The advisory notes "No patched version has been released" as of 2026-06-18. The underlying
      SQLite CVE is fixed in libsqlite >= 3.50.2 but the SQLitePCLRaw wrapper has not been rebuilt.
      Pulled transitively by Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite (10.0.7), which the solution ships
      as an optional provider swap and uses in test projects. Production runs on PostgreSQL
      (Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL) — SQLite is not exposed to production traffic.
      Revisit when SQLitePCLRaw publishes a rebuilt package (>= 2.1.12) and remove this entry.

    SixLabors.ImageSharp 3.1.12 CVE cluster — all five fixed in 4.1.2, but 4.x now gates on a
    paid Six Labors license at build time (`error : No Six Labors license found. Set
    $(SixLaborsLicenseKey)…`). Upgrading without purchasing a license is not possible.
    ImageSharp usage in this codebase is narrow: WorkInstructionFileService loads work-instruction
    media files from the server's own WebRootPath (curated by technicians via the WI editor) and
    re-encodes them as PNG for an Excel export. Not an attacker-controlled TIFF/BigTIFF input path,
    so the real-world risk of these CVEs is low here. Revisit if (a) a Six Labors license is
    purchased, or (b) a 3.x patch release is backported, or (c) the usage is migrated to an
    alternative library (SkiaSharp, System.Drawing.Common on Windows).
      GHSA-gwg2-r3hj-4w44 (moderate)
      GHSA-wmxv-xphr-5c9g (moderate)
      GHSA-j3p4-wp97-rph4 (high)
      GHSA-j9gm-c75j-xc9q (high)
      GHSA-jjfr-hcj7-qf5w (high)
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gwg2-r3hj-4w44" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wmxv-xphr-5c9g" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j3p4-wp97-rph4" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j9gm-c75j-xc9q" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jjfr-hcj7-qf5w" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
